# REFERENCE — the documentation map

> **Purpose: THE MAP.** The permanent map of the whole documentation repository:
> the structure of every doc, key facts, conventions, and the links between them. An
> agent or dev **consults this first** for any doc work — it saves context and keeps
> facts from leaking. **Written LAST** (Phase 10), then maintained on every doc change.
>
> **Rule:** before reading/editing any `.md` — check its card in §3. Before creating a
> new doc — check it isn't already covered (§3), then add a card for it here.

## 1. Repository map
> The tree of the repo from docs' point-of-view, with one-line purpose per entry.
> (Point to the real layout — do NOT drift from actual folders.)

```
<repo>/
├── README.md            # EN-overview, structure, status
├── ENTRY.md             # entry point: topics → files (start here)
├── AGENT.md             # runbook (agent phases, rules, DoD) (L2+)
├── DELIVERY.md          # what ships, how to verify, what's NOT in (L2+)
├── docs/
│   ├── REFERENCE.md     # ★ THIS FILE — map
│   ├── ARCHITECTURE.md  # components, communication, data flow
│   ├── FEATURES.md      # module/feature catalog + ✅/📋
│   ├── SAGA.md          # cross-module scenarios (L3·microservices)
│   ├── TEST_CASES.md    # Gherkin cases + coverage matrix
│   ├── DEV_GUIDE.md     # local run/env/debug/add-module
│   ├── IMPROVEMENTS.md  # known issues + fix plans
│   ├── TROUBLESHOOTING.md # error diagnostics E1…En + checklist
│   ├── BACKLOG.md       # ideas/deferred/priorities
│   ├── REVIEW.md        # doc audit + per-module status matrix
│   └── ADR/ADR-00N.md   # ADR records (ADR-007 = canonical convention L2+)
├── contracts/           # machine truth — openapi/, asyncapi/ (L3)
└── services/            # implementation
```

## 2. Hierarchy of truth (canon)
> On any conflict the top wins. 🔻 rank 1 = highest authority.
1. **Canon ADR** (e.g. `docs/ADR/ADR-007.md`) — consolidated conventions.
2. **`AGENT.md` / `DELIVERY.md`** — operational rules, gate.
3. **`contracts/`** (openapi + asyncapi) — exact API/event truth.
4. **Narrative docs** (ARCHITECTURE, DEV_GUIDE, FEATURES, SAGA, TEST_CASES).
5. **Shared code types** (`@<scope>/shared`) — the code fact.

> A drift (README vs reality) is recorded in §5 + `docs/IMPROVEMENTS.md`, not silently.

## 3. Per-file documentation cards
> Format: **purpose → structure → key facts → links**. One short card per doc.
### 3.x `<doc>` 
- **Purpose:** …
- **Structure:** …
- **Key facts:** … (numbers that must stay true — tests, counts)
- **Links:** points to …, is pointed by …
_(Add a card for each document you create — README/ENTRY/ARCHITECTURE/FEATURES/SAGA/
REVIEW/TEST_CASES/DEV_GUIDE/IMPROVEMENTS/TROUBLESHOOTING/BACKLOG + each ADR.)_

### 3.x ADR
| ADR | Topic | Status |
|-----|-------|--------|
| ADR-001 | … | active |
| ADR-007 | **canon** — supersedes 002…006 | **canon** |

## 4. Known drifts (doc-vs-fact) — control list
| # | Where | The drift | Who's right (source) |
|---|-------|-----------|----------------------|
| 4.x | e.g. README counts | deviates from actual grep | `docs/FEATURES.md` fact |
> Each drift has a fix plan in `docs/IMPROVEMENTS.md`; keep this table in sync.

## 5. Commands (reference; verify in DEV_GUIDE)
```bash
pnpm test           # unit (no storage)
pnpm test:contract  # conformance
docker compose --profile core up -d   # infra
```

## 6. Routing table "where to look"
| Question | First place |
|----------|-------------|
| What is this project | `ENTRY.md` → `README.md` |
| Architecture/sagas | `ARCHITECTURE.md` → `SAGA.md` (see ADR-00N) |
| Conventions/canon | `ADR-00N` (canon) |
| API of module X | `contracts/openapi/<x>.yaml` |
| Events | `contracts/asyncapi/events.yaml` + `SAGA.md` |
| Feature status | `FEATURES.md` |
| How to run | `DEV_GUIDE.md` |
| Known problems / plan | `IMPROVEMENTS.md` |
| Error when running | `TROUBLESHOOTING.md` |
| Backlog | `BACKLOG.md` |
| Doc audit / per-module | `REVIEW.md` |

## 7. How to maintain this file
- Change any doc → update its card in §3.
- New drift → add a row in §4 + plan in IMPROVEMENTS.
- New ADR → add to §3.x table; new module → §4/(FEATURES) + §3 card
> Keep cards as echoes — the **compressed** structure/facts/links, not copies.